ind":"announcement","title":"v0.10.27: Cut Stars and a Patient Rival","summary":"The cut grade could call a good cut poor, because it was guessing at what the rival threw into the crib. It now counts only what you can see, shows as stars, and explains itself when you ask. The Hard and Expert rivals also stop spending the consumables they play before the throw on the first hand. Added The cut grade now shows as five stars. Point at them, or hold Space or the right trigger, and they stay up while a small card explains the grade, with how many of the other cards would have done","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-24T14:39:46Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114039775","verified_at":"2026-10-24T17:40:43Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4783460-1847286114028861","game_id":"steam-4783460","kind":"announcement","title":"v0.10.26: Mac Speed and Clearer Clubs","summary":"Version 0.10.25 slowed the match table badly on Macs, and I wanted that fixed fast. This patch puts the Mac back on its old graphics path, smooths out the opening climb, and gives the club one more redraw. Improved The club is redrawn as a clover, with deep notches between its three leaves and a thin stem, so it is much harder to mistake for a spade, even on the smallest cards where it used to blur into a blob. The Events log now prints suits in the same shapes as the cards, instead of borrowing","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-21T13:26:24Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114028861","verified_at":"2026-10-21T18:44:22Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4783460-1847286114026902","game_id":"steam-4783460","kind":"announcement","title":"v0.10.24: The Mountain and the Count","summary":"This patch is about how a match feels. A lot of the table used to react before the card or peg that earned it had landed, so I went through the match beat by beat and put every sound and move in order, and the opening is now a climb up the mountain you are about to play. There is also a round of readability fixes so the table reads by light and dark, not only by color. Improved The opening is now a climb of about 30 seconds up the mountain, over rolling hills for each region of the Long Tally, e","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-20T22:33:02Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114026902","verified_at":"2026-10-21T08:07:13Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4783460-1846651706696853","game_id":"steam-4783460","kind":"announcement","title":"v0.10.25: Card Legibility","summary":"Playtest feedback said the hand read small and busy, and that clubs looked a lot like spades. So this release is a pass over the card faces. Added Face cards print their rank a second time on a small plate in the bottom-left corner. When cards overlap on the played row and hide their right side, you can still tell a jack from a queen from a king. Improved The marks inside each card are about half again as big, and a corner rank sits closer to its suit so the two read as one. Face cards now show ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-20T21:57:51Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706696853","verified_at":"2026-10-21T08:07:13Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4783460-1846651706691327","game_id":"steam-4783460","kind":"announcement","title":"Double Skunk is in Steam Next Fest","summary":"Steam Next Fest runs until October 26, and the free Double Skunk demo is part of it. What's in the demo You play five rivals on the way to the Parlor Cup, and Big Brenda is the last of them. Each match starts with you picking a powerup and a consumable (a one-use card), and partway around each board you can stop at the Pedlar's shop. Never played cribbage? Choose How to Play and the Coach will teach you. {STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/46147149/510303c56b8bc5b807236ac28a73046f8edf250e.gif The weekly challeng","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-19T17:00:42Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706691327","verified_at":"2026-10-20T17:04:24Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4783460-1846651706677468","game_id":"steam-4783460","kind":"announcement","title":"v0.10.23: Lap Gold and House Scores","summary":"I wanted every lap shop in a weekly challenge to give you a choice. It used to open with an empty purse, so selling your cards back was all you could do there. Added Weekly challenges and practice runs now pay 10 gold each time your peg finishes a lap. Your peg stops at the gate, the gold flies to your purse, and the lap shop opens with something to spend. Because this changes scores, this version plays on a fresh weekly board, so scores posted on an older version are not on it, and a weekly or ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-15T12:22:15Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706677468","verified_at":"2026-10-20T17:04:24Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4783460-1846651706672882","game_id":"steam-4783460","kind":"announcement","title":"v0.10.22: A home for the weekly challenge","summary":"I measured the ten weekly challenges. For a player who didn't build around the kit, eight leaned hard toward the rival and two leaned hard the other way, so I rebuilt every kit. The challenges were also hard to find and needed the online board to play at all, so they now have their own page and you can practice any of them offline. Added Weekly challenges have a page of their own. On the main menu, vs. AI now asks whether you want to set the table or play a challenge. The page shows this week's ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-14T01:26:52Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706672882","verified_at":"2026-10-20T17:04:24Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4783460-1846018067944784","game_id":"steam-4783460","kind":"announcement","title":"Dev diary: how the warm-up teaches cribbage in two hands","summary":"Cribbage has a reputation for being hard to learn. The rules are easy enough. The hard part is counting your hand. You add up fifteens, pairs, runs and flushes all at once, out loud, while your opponent listens for anything you missed. So I made the warm-up skip the rules talk and deal you a hand. Hand one is the Coach's The Coach plays the first hand with you, one short step at a time. Each step lights up whatever the Coach is talking about, like your discards, the cut card, the count or your p","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-13T17:00:24Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067944784","verified_at":"2026-10-20T17:04:24Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4783460-1845383656393698","game_id":"steam-4783460","kind":"announcement","title":"The free Double Skunk demo is out now","summary":"The free demo of Double Skunk is out now. It's the real game, but the campaign stops at the Parlor Cup. What's in it Five rivals. Aunt Beryl Buns, Sergeant Snip, Tatty Topaz, Cousin Mab, and Big Brenda, who keeps the Parlor Cup on top of her fridge. Powerups and consumables. Every campaign match starts with you picking a powerup and a consumable (a one-use card). The demo has some of the powerups and all of the consumables. The weekly challenge. Everyone gets the same deal each week, and the dem","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-05T15:00:42Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1845383656393698","verified_at":"2026-10-20T17:04:24Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-4783460":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T04:23:27Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-26T04:23:27Z","error_codes":[]}},"news_last_attempt_at":{"steam-4783460":"2026-10-26T04:23:27Z"},"notices":[],"news_sources":{"4783460":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T04:23:27Z","last_success_at":"2026-10-26T04:23:27Z","status":"ok","error_codes":[]},"5262890":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T04:23:27Z","last_success_at":"2026-10-26T04:23:27Z","status":"ok","error_codes":[]}},"context_snapshots":[{"schema_version":1,"game_id":"steam-4783460","app_id":4783460,"app_scope":"base","observed_at":"2026-10-26T06:14:57Z","source_url":"https://api.steampowered.com/IStoreBrowseService/GetItems/v1/","context":{"country":"KR","language":"koreana","batch_size":100},"status":"ok","error_code":null,"store_item_success":1,"raw_item_sha256":"ef5ca0696bca749fb511e052d4d6d46210315c468a76111619e5f3fea794de54","response_sha256":null,"source_fields":{"basic_info":{"short_description":"Double Skunk is a cribbage roguelite. Powerups change what your count pays, and one-shot cards can shove the rival's peg back. Climb a ladder of named rivals, then play the weekly deal everyone shares, or take on a friend online.","publishers":[{"name":"Kerrberry Systems"}],"developers":[{"name":"Kerrberry Games","creator_clan_account_id":46526371}]},"release":{"steam_release_date":1793836860,"is_coming_